Article 3
This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children in the region;
b. prevent the occurrence of actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and children;
c. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for victims of violence;
e. provide services to victims of violence; and
f. carry out comprehensive recovery for victims of violence.

Article 14
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 3 include:
a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential; b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women; c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage; e. facilitating and endeavoring to preserve customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge regarding independent, healthy and prosperous family planning; g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the Region;

Article 11
(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point at each OPD as referred to in Article 9 letter l consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or program duties.
(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the following duties:
a. promoting Gender Mainstreaming in the work unit;
b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of OPD that are gender responsive;
c. implementing training, socialization, advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the OPD environment;
d. reporting the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming to the leadership of the OPD;
e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in the work unit; and
f. facilitating the preparation of gender data at each OPD;
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and determined by the leadership of the OPD.

Article 5
(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:
a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Region;
c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region;
d. enhancing Women's Empowerment in roles, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.
e. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for Women's Empowerment in the Region;
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 21
In order to prevent acts of violence against women and Children, the community:
a. monitors various conditions occurring in its environment that may give rise to violations of the rights of women and children;
b. increases awareness of violations of the rights of women and children;
c. strengthens the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment; and
d. prevents unregistered marriages and marriage at child age.

Article 20
(1) In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. involves community participation in recovery and reintegration; d. develops an integrated database and information system regarding acts of violence against women and children;
e. develops family empowerment programs;
f. strengthens the function of community organizations engaged in women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and
h. peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

